          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:03c87e67a462e6d3d093a26c84a7a7c3681ef7d55db0b1bc690e4384b62f3e78:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8ae7a38a2eec47c59e6860bacc6be537",
      "statement": "Every rejection the store raises is its own Error naming the session or the root and carrying the underlying failure as cause, except a wrong-schemaVersion or wrong-identifier rejection which carries no cause and names both the found and the expected value; the temporary .tmp names never appear in a message.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/server/src/adapters/session-store/filesystem-session-store.ts#L235-L266",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4531cb9887e97e04316a99fdd48d3589d87fd6a3525f180bc3ce1aad39379945:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/server/src/adapters/session-store/filesystem-session-store.ts#L301-L320",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:20cac1374805db4664c50f4934abe55d1bcdf4dd0ecae2ddf658b135785bc68c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://specs/adapters/filesystem-session-store/spec.md#L83-L90",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:47bd75afccabc92170b8252768ef0291d03683df384f8b5b01e40835faba7406:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6b2bf7a18a9143e6bff826b0186e8fba",
      "statement": "isStorableIdentifier requires a single path segment (non-empty, not . or .., no /, \\, or NUL byte) and is checked by save, load, and list alike; save of a rejected identifier throws naming it and writes nothing, load resolves undefined, and list omits a directory so named.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/server/src/adapters/session-store/filesystem-session-store.ts#L282-L306",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6163d23a399d81029445a39e324635f71bfa3a64783ccd8a05547714231b3a6f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://specs/adapters/filesystem-session-store/spec.md#L79-L90",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b25a7f336204691426a85fa357ead09d37e2a1e5df272a61ec19a51f622f006f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_af86c4a034f94c918164e2e159c07900",
      "statement": "save stages each file under <target>.<randomUUID()>.tmp in the target directory, calls handle.sync() as a durability barrier before any rename, then renames both onto their targets with session.json first; a failure before the renames discards every staged file and leaves the previous revision exactly as the last successful save left it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/server/src/adapters/session-store/filesystem-session-store.ts#L361-L444",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:de9f3d1bb72d7ec84b41e9070669305c53386355791f20a9df609bfb5068025b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://specs/_decision/003-add-filesystem-session-store.md#L57-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5d581c32a2f775b660fcc626aaf632bbd9b73c073f0d784d3b09ecb9fa278e38:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e570a6e84a494a2b93d9b833c2a62706",
      "statement": "The store deliberately does not fsync the session directory or root after the renames: a lost rename leaves the previous revision whole, the same outcome as a save that never ran, and the only residue a failure between the two renames can leave is a transcript lagging its state.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/server/src/adapters/session-store/filesystem-session-store.ts#L361-L375",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bfee9f4465cafa19e67a75fea692ca3481e1b31134e5a3c3fa1925c4b53843f1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://specs/_decision/003-add-filesystem-session-store.md#L71-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e2d1b5489aaf7549fa13b4feada3a49df569e6b420b17764a7a71cb899f4bab0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_47daa32415d04d4a91029bb4e58eac2a",
      "statement": "Every directory the store creates is mode 0o700 and every file 0o600, set at creation via mkdir mode and open mode and carried onto targets by rename, because a session holds unpublished product ideas and the default umask would expose them to every account on the machine.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/server/src/adapters/session-store/filesystem-session-store.ts#L17-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ac923115243dc2663e9e6e82be91706de0e824c3b300d041f02abc03505307f6:"
        },
        {
